# Slice 285: a `sub` returns no value and has three parts, args, var and body: no result part, so `s\return` names nothing (the book,
# #method-parts: "the description of the return where there is one").  The refusal is the path's: unknown field path segment.
sub: s ()
    int: w 2
end: s
int: n s\return
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: 7; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
